    },
    "body": "The v1 query/prefix continuation factor cannot overcome frozen Copy competition on ten of the 32 retained development entries: the exact integer range diagnostic relaxes coefficient correlations and checks every possible common clipped reference. This change gives the same signed-H4 token energy to Generate and every physical Copy occurrence before the existing single clip, with a versioned dyadic score scale. It keeps v1 artifact loading and the ordinary full alias pool.\n\nThe existing Rust fitter gains a continuation-only mode with an authenticated immutable Source48/Generate64 parent, only 960 trainable coefficients, all-answer/EOS credit and independent saved-artifact own-feedback evaluation. Fixed teacher-prefix caches call the production native generator and admit no current target, answer-bearing selected record or mask. Labels enter only the objective. CPU/CUDA transfer accounting includes Copy gather indices; fully resident alias reduction remains separate.\n\nIndependent source reviews approve the fitter/cache and v2 arithmetic. Both package checks, 32 focused CPU tests and two explicit CUDA score/gradient controls passed (per-head evidence in the review comment). The full-answer construction fit is running; learned prediction is not yet established. Zero-field v1 replay and CUDA evidence from #1855 remain separately bound; they do not count as v2 execution. The optimistic independent per-token v2 envelope wins32/32, which is a necessary score-support check, not a jointly realizable field or prediction result.\n\nReferences #820.\n",
