      "body": "Exact-head self-review: c64cce4f2fc76cd8534a945184223fab0f3065a5.\n\nReviewed clean merge of main3f6adaf preserving DeepSeek's latest fitter/declared-panel work. Independent continuation reviewer rechecked the merged fitter: continuation parent/cache/training/evaluation, argument guards and soft deadline behavior are byte-identical to5c6fad2. No conflicting continuation behavior found. Core and training/src are byte-identical across those heads (checked with git diff).\n\nActual validation on Linux x86_64:\n- At5c6fad2: core/check, training CUDA-feature check; native field5, native bank7, training field7, training bank11, fitter2 focused CPU tests all PASS (32 total). Ignored CUDA tests were not counted.\n- At c64cce4: both package checks rerun PASS; merged fitter two tests PASS; release CUDA-feature fitter build PASS; changed-file Rustfmt, diff check and claim-wording PASS. Prior unchanged library tests reused at their exact identity.\n- Full cargo fmt --check attempted: nine inherited files fail (six addressed-attention bins, entry-scorer-feasibility.rs, mqar-bench.rs, relation_compiler.rs), none a PR-touched file. No unrelated format edits.\n- Executed on leased RTX4090 lg5m36pkj563my / CUDA12.8: continuation_cuda_shared_action_units_and_copy_adjoint_match_cpu PASS; continuation_cuda_shared_copy_native_anchor_and_duplicate_adjoint_match_cpu PASS. Explicit --ignored --exact invocations each report1pass, total2. Durations6.70s and0.20s include first CUDA setup. Component parity, not whole-model CUDA parity/quality.\n\nHF source/binary/checks revision f3be21f2d96dec3e4d5e4038310c901bff5aa699, codex/native-continuation-field/fit-runtime-c64cce4/; freshly downloaded all files and SHA256 verified on the actual test pod. Test executable SHA0af64c4d3942f02c15dfc9825930501d59f0eba1ad8d5634c7adcd63f380c9d0 (built5c, unchanged library source); fitter SHA2f9be70d052220f584c57921eef53a9cfef5e27242e811f03c6e4b113e346d68 (built c64). Pod checks receipt at /worksp